## Docker Compose 

    Docker Compose is a tool that lets you run multiple containers together using one YAML file instead of typing long docker run commands.

    Think of it as:
        “A single blueprint that defines your entire application stack.”
    
    Example:
    A real app usually needs:
    • a backend container
    • a database container
    • a cache container
    • a frontend container
    Compose lets you start all of them with:

        "docker compose up" 


## Why Docker Compose Exists (The Problem It Solves)

    Without Compose:
        • You manually run each container
        • You manually link networks
        • You manually mount volumes
        • You manually pass environment variables
        • You manually restart everything
        With Compose:
        • One file
        • One command
        • Everything works together

## The Heart of Compose: `docker-compose.yml`
    This YAML file describes:
        • services (containers)
        • images to use
        • ports to expose
        • volumes to persist data
        • networks to connect services
        • environment variables
        • dependencies between containers

        